[ti:Down by the Salley Gardens]
[ar:Traditional]
[01:00.00]Down by the salley gardens my love and I did meet
[01:25.04]She passed the salley gardens with little snow-white feet
[01:55.04]She bid me take love easy, as the leaves grow on the tree
[02:12.08]But I, being young and foolish, with her would not agree
[02:25.12]In a field by the river my love and I did stand
[02:54.16]And on my leaning shoulder she laid her snow-white hand
[03:23.20]She bid me take life easy, as the grass grows on the weirs
[03:44.24]But I was young and foolish, and now am full of tears
